\s1 Jonah Flees from the LORD
\r (\ref Nahum 1:1–15|NAM 1:1-15\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amittai|אֲמִתַּ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Get up|ק֠וּם\rb*! \rb Go|לֵ֧ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Nineveh|נִֽינְוֵ֛ה\rb* \rb and preach|וּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb its wickedness|רָעָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb has come up|עָלְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Jonah, however|יוֹנָה֙\rb*, \rb got up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb to flee|לִבְרֹ֣חַ\rb* \rb to Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֔ישָׁה\rb*, \rb away from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He went down|וַיֵּ֨רֶד\rb* \rb to Joppa|יָפ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb a ship|אָנִיָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb bound|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb for Tarshish|תַרְשִׁ֗ישׁ\rb*. \rb So he paid|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the fare|שְׂכָרָ֜הּ\rb* \rb and went aboard|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb*\rb |בָּהּ֙\rb* \rb to sail|לָב֤וֹא\rb*\rb |עִמָּהֶם֙\rb* \rb for Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֔ישָׁה\rb*, \rb away from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Great Storm
\r (\ref Acts 27:13–26|ACT 27:13-26\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Then the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb hurled|הֵטִ֤יל\rb* \rb a great|גְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb wind|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb and such a violent|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb storm|סַֽעַר־\rb* \rb arose|וַיְהִ֥י\rb*\rb |בַּיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb that the ship|וְהָ֣אֳנִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb was in danger|חִשְּׁבָ֖ה\rb* \rb of breaking apart|לְהִשָּׁבֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb The sailors|הַמַּלָּחִ֗ים\rb* \rb were afraid|וַיִּֽירְא֣וּ\rb*, \rb and each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb cried out|וַֽיִּזְעֲקוּ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own god|אֱלֹהָיו֒\rb*. \rb And they threw|וַיָּטִ֨לוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ship’s|בָּֽאֳנִיָּה֙\rb* \rb cargo|הַכֵּלִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb to lighten|לְהָקֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the load|מֵֽעֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb But Jonah|וְיוֹנָ֗ה\rb* \rb had gone down|יָרַד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the lowest part|יַרְכְּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the vessel|הַסְּפִינָ֔ה\rb*, \rb where he lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb and fell into a deep sleep|וַיֵּרָדַֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb The captain|רַ֣ב\rb*\rb |הַחֹבֵ֔ל\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּקְרַ֤ב\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb can you|לְּךָ֣\rb* \rb sleep|נִרְדָּ֑ם\rb*? \rb Get up|ק֚וּם\rb* \rb and call|קְרָ֣א\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֞י\rb* \rb this God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb will consider|יִתְעַשֵּׁ֧ת\rb* \rb us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb so that|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb we may not perish|נֹאבֵֽד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 “\rb Come|לְכוּ֙\rb*!” \rb said the sailors|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one another|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb*. “\rb Let us cast|וְנַפִּ֣ילָה\rb* \rb lots|גֽוֹרָל֔וֹת\rb* \rb to find out|וְנֵ֣דְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb who is responsible|בְּשֶׁלְּמִ֛י\rb* \rb for this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb calamity|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb that is upon us|לָ֑נוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb So they cast|וַיַּפִּ֙לוּ֙\rb* \rb lots|גּֽוֹרָל֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the lot|הַגּוֹרָ֖ל\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb Tell|הַגִּידָה־\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb now|נָּ֣א\rb*,” \rb they demanded|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb who|לְמִי־\rb* \rb is to blame|בַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb for this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb calamity|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb that is upon us|לָ֑נוּ\rb*? \rb What is|מַה־\rb* \rb your occupation|מְּלַאכְתְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb and where|וּמֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb have you come from|תָּב֔וֹא\rb*? \rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb is your country|אַרְצֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and who|וְאֵֽי־\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb are your|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb people|עַ֖ם\rb*?”
\p \v 9 “\rb I am|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb a Hebrew|עִבְרִ֣י\rb*,” \rb replied Jonah|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb worship|יָרֵ֔א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the dry land|הַיַּבָּשָֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Then the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb were even more|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb afraid|וַיִּֽירְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |יִרְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb*?” \rb The men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb knew|יָדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb was fleeing|בֹרֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he had told|הִגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Jonah Cast into the Sea
\p \v 11 \rb Now|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb was growing worse|הוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and worse|וְסֹעֵֽר׃\rb*, \rb so they said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to Jonah|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb must we do|נַּ֣עֲשֶׂה\rb* \rb to you|לָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to calm|וְיִשְׁתֹּ֥ק\rb* \rb this sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb for us|מֵֽעָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*?”
\p \v 12 “\rb Pick me up|שָׂא֙וּנִי֙\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* “\rb and cast me|וַהֲטִילֻ֣נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb so it|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb may quiet down|וְיִשְׁתֹּ֥ק\rb* \rb for you|מֵֽעֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb know|יוֹדֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I am to blame|בְשֶׁלִּ֔י\rb* \rb for this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb violent|הַגָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb storm|הַסַּ֧עַר\rb* \rb that has come upon you|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Nevertheless, the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb rowed hard|וַיַּחְתְּר֣וּ\rb*\f + \fr 1:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa the men dug in\f* \rb to get back|לְהָשִׁ֛יב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb dry land|הַיַּבָּשָׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb but they|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb could not|יָכֹ֑לוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb was raging|וְסֹעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb more and more|הוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb So they cried out|וַיִּקְרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*: “\rb Please|אָנָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb let us perish|נֹאבְדָ֗ה\rb* \rb on account of this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb man’s|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb life|בְּנֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb*! \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb charge|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb with innocent|נָקִ֑יא\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֣ם\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb have done|עָשִֽׂיתָ׃\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You pleased|חָפַ֖צְתָּ\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then they picked up|וַיִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and cast him|וַיְטִלֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the raging|מִזַּעְפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb grew calm|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Then the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |יִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּֽירְא֧וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb greatly|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and they offered|וַיִּֽזְבְּחוּ־\rb* \rb a sacrifice|זֶ֙בַח֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and made|וַֽיִּדְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb vows to Him|נְדָרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had appointed|וַיְמַ֤ן\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb fish|דָּ֣ג\rb* \rb to swallow|לִבְלֹ֖עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Jonah|יוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb spent|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb nights|לֵילֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb in the belly|בִּמְעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the fish|הַדָּ֔ג\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Jonah’s Prayer
\p \v 1 \rb From inside|מִמְּעֵ֖י\rb* \rb the fish|הַדָּגָֽה׃\rb*, \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb*, \v 2 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb In my distress|מִצָּ֥רָה\rb* \rb I called|קָ֠רָאתִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He answered me|וַֽיַּעֲנֵ֑נִי\rb*.
\q1 \rb From the belly|מִבֶּ֧טֶן\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁא֛וֹל\rb* \rb I called for help|שִׁוַּ֖עְתִּי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and You heard|שָׁמַ֥עְתָּ\rb* \rb my voice|קוֹלִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb For You cast me|וַתַּשְׁלִיכֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb into the deep|מְצוּלָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb into the heart|בִּלְבַ֣ב\rb* \rb of the seas|יַמִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb and the current|וְנָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb swirled about me|יְסֹבְבֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Your breakers|מִשְׁבָּרֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and waves|וְגַלֶּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb swept|עָבָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb over me|עָלַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb At this, I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb I have been banished|נִגְרַ֖שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb from|מִנֶּ֣גֶד\rb* \rb Your sight|עֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*;
\q1 \rb yet|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb I will look|לְהַבִּ֔יט\rb* \rb once more|אוֹסִ֣יף\rb*
\q2 \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your holy|קָדְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb temple|הֵיכַ֖ל\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The waters|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb engulfed me|אֲפָפ֤וּנִי\rb*
\q2 \rb to take|עַד־\rb* \rb my life|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb*;
\q1 \rb the watery depths|תְּה֖וֹם\rb* \rb closed around me|יְסֹבְבֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb the seaweed|ס֖וּף\rb* \rb wrapped|חָב֥וּשׁ\rb* \rb around my head|לְרֹאשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb To the roots|לְקִצְבֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the mountains|הָרִים֙\rb* \rb I descended|יָרַ֔דְתִּי\rb*;
\q2 \rb the earth|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb beneath me|בַעֲדִ֖י\rb* \rb barred me in|בְּרִחֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*!
\q1 \rb But You raised|וַתַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb my life|חַיַּ֖י\rb* \rb from the pit|מִשַּׁ֛חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb As my life|נַפְשִׁ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was fading away|בְּהִתְעַטֵּ֤ף\rb*\rb |עָלַי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb I remembered|זָכָ֑רְתִּי\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb My prayer|תְּפִלָּתִ֔י\rb* \rb went up|וַתָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your holy|קָדְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb temple|הֵיכַ֖ל\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Those who cling to|מְשַׁמְּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb worthless|שָׁ֑וְא\rb* \rb idols|הַבְלֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb forsake|יַעֲזֹֽבוּ׃\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדָּ֖ם\rb*.\f + \fr 2:8 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f*
\q1 \v 9 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb*, \rb with the voice|בְּק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of thanksgiving|תּוֹדָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb will sacrifice|אֶזְבְּחָה־\rb* \rb to You|לָּ֔ךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will fulfill|אֲשַׁלֵּ֑מָה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have vowed|נָדַ֖רְתִּי\rb*.
\q2 \rb Salvation|יְשׁוּעָ֖תָה\rb* \rb is from the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 10 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the fish|לַדָּ֑ג\rb*, \rb and it vomited|וַיָּקֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb onto|אֶל־\rb* \rb dry land|הַיַּבָּשָֽׁה׃פ\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 The Ninevites Repent
\r (\ref Matthew 12:38–42|MAT 12:38-42\ref*; \ref Luke 11:29–32|LUK 11:29-32\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֥ית\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 2 “\rb Get up|ק֛וּם\rb*! \rb Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Nineveh|נִֽינְוֵ֖ה\rb* \rb and proclaim|וִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to it|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the message|הַקְּרִיאָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb give|דֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb This time Jonah|יוֹנָ֗ה\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nineveh|נִֽינְוֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb in accordance with the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb Now Nineveh|וְנִֽינְוֵ֗ה\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb an exceedingly|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb great|גְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb city|עִיר־\rb*,\f + \fr 3:3 \ft Or \fqa was a great city to God\f* \rb requiring a three-day|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb journey|מַהֲלַ֖ךְ\rb*.\f + \fr 3:3 \ft Literally \fqa great city, a three-day journey\f* \v 4 \rb On the first|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of his journey|מַהֲלַ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb Jonah|יוֹנָה֙\rb*\rb |לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֤חֶל\rb* \rb into the city|בָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and proclaimed|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb more|ע֚וֹד\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and Nineveh|וְנִֽינְוֵ֖ה\rb* \rb will be overturned|נֶהְפָּֽכֶת׃\rb*!”
\p \v 5 \rb |אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb And the Ninevites|נִֽינְוֵ֖ה\rb* \rb believed|וַֽיַּאֲמִ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb God|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb They proclaimed|וַיִּקְרְאוּ־\rb* \rb a fast|צוֹם֙\rb* \rb and dressed|וַיִּלְבְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb in sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb from the greatest|מִגְּדוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb of them to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the least|קְטַנָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When word|הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb reached|וַיִּגַּ֤ע\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶך\rb* \rb of Nineveh|נִֽינְוֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb he got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb from his throne|מִכִּסְא֔וֹ\rb*, \rb took off|וַיַּעֲבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb his royal robe|אַדַּרְתּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb covered himself|וַיְכַ֣ס\rb* \rb with sackcloth|שַׂ֔ק\rb*, \rb and sat|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb in|מֵֽעָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb ashes|הָאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then he issued a proclamation|וַיַּזְעֵ֗ק\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb in Nineveh|בְּנִֽינְוֵ֔ה\rb*:
\pmo “\rb By the decree|מִטַּ֧עַם\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his nobles|וּגְדֹלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\pmo \rb Let no|אַֽל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֨ם\rb* \rb or beast|וְהַבְּהֵמָ֜ה\rb*, \rb herd|הַבָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb or flock|וְהַצֹּ֗אן\rb*, \rb taste|יִטְעֲמוּ֙\rb* \rb anything at all|מְא֔וּמָה\rb*. \rb They must not|אַ֨ל־\rb* \rb eat|יִרְע֔וּ\rb* \rb or drink|יִשְׁתּֽוּ׃\rb*\rb |וּמַ֖יִם\rb*.\rb |אַל־\rb* \v 8 \rb Furthermore, let both man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb and beast|וְהַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb be covered|וְיִתְכַּסּ֣וּ\rb* \rb with sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb and have everyone call out|וְיִקְרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb earnestly|בְּחָזְקָ֑ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Let each one|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb turn|וְיָשֻׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb his evil|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and from the violence|הֶחָמָ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in his hands|בְּכַפֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֣עַ\rb*? \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb may turn|יָשׁ֔וּב\rb* \rb and relent|וְנִחַ֖ם\rb*; \rb He may turn|וְשָׁ֛ב\rb* \rb from His fierce|מֵחֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb anger|אַפּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb so that we will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb perish|נֹאבֵֽד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb When God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb their actions|מַ֣עֲשֵׂיהֶ֔ם\rb*— \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb they had turned|שָׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb from their evil|הָרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכָּ֣ם\rb*— \rb He|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb relented|וַיִּנָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had threatened|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to bring|לַעֲשׂוֹת־\rb* \rb upon them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Jonah’s Anger at the LORD’s Compassion
\p \v 1 \rb Jonah, however|יוֹנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb was greatly|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb displeased|וַיֵּ֥רַע\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |רָעָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and he became angry|וַיִּ֖חַר\rb*.\f + \fr 4:1 \ft Or \fqa It was exceedingly evil to Jonah, and he became angry\f* \v 2 \rb So he prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb O|אָנָּ֤ה\rb* \rb LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb is this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb what I said|דְבָרִ֗י\rb* \rb while|עַד־\rb* \rb I was|הֱיוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb still in|עַל־\rb* \rb my own country|אַדְמָתִ֔י\rb*? \rb This is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I was so quick|קִדַּ֖מְתִּי\rb* \rb to flee|לִבְרֹ֣חַ\rb* \rb toward Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֑ישָׁה\rb*. \rb I knew|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You are|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb a gracious|חַנּ֣וּן\rb* \rb and compassionate|וְרַח֔וּם\rb* \rb God|אֵֽל־\rb*, \rb slow|אֶ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb to anger|אַפַּ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb abounding|וְרַב־\rb* \rb in loving devotion|חֶ֔סֶד\rb* — \rb One who relents|וְנִחָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb sending disaster|הָרָעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb please|נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb take|קַח־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it is better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb for me to die|מוֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb than to live|מֵחַיָּֽי׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Have you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb any right|הַהֵיטֵ֖ב\rb* \rb to be angry|חָ֥רָה\rb*?”
\p \v 5 \rb Then Jonah|יוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and sat down|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb east|מִן־\rb* \rb of it|מִקֶּ֣דֶם\rb*\rb |לָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb where|שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּעַשׂ֩\rb* \rb himself|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb a shelter|סֻכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֶּ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb in its shade|בַּצֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb see|יִרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb would happen|יִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the city|בָּעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֠לֹהִים\rb* \rb appointed|וַיְמַ֣ן\rb* \rb a vine|קִיקָי֞וֹן\rb*,\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa qiqayon\ft ; that is, possibly the castor oil plant; also in verses 7, 9, and 10 \f* \rb and it grew up|וַיַּ֣עַל׀\rb* \rb to provide|לִֽהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb shade|צֵל֙\rb* \rb over|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb Jonah’s|לְיוֹנָ֗ה\rb* \rb head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to ease|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb discomfort|מֵרָֽעָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and Jonah|יוֹנָ֛ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb was greatly|שִׂמְחָ֥ה\rb*\rb |גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּשְׂמַ֥ח\rb* \rb with the plant|הַקִּֽיקָי֖וֹן\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb When dawn|הַשַּׁ֖חַר\rb* \rb came|בַּעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb the next day|לַֽמָּחֳרָ֑ת\rb*, \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb appointed|וַיְמַ֤ן\rb* \rb a worm|תּוֹלַ֔עַת\rb* \rb that attacked|וַתַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plant|הַקִּֽיקָי֖וֹן\rb* \rb so that it withered|וַיִּיבָֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb As the sun|הַשֶּׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb* \rb was rising|כִּזְרֹ֣חַ\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb appointed|וַיְמַ֨ן\rb* \rb a scorching|חֲרִישִׁ֔ית\rb* \rb east|קָדִים֙\rb* \rb wind|ר֤וּחַ\rb*, \rb and the sun|הַשֶּׁ֛מֶשׁ\rb* \rb beat down|וַתַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Jonah’s|יוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb so that he grew faint|וַיִּתְעַלָּ֑ף\rb*\rb |נַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb and wished|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֔וּת\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb It is better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb for me to die|מוֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb than to live|מֵחַיָּֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Have you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb any right|הַהֵיטֵ֥ב\rb* \rb to be angry|חָרָֽה־\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the plant|הַקִּֽיקָי֑וֹן\rb*?”
\p “\rb I do|הֵיטֵ֥ב\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I am angry|חָֽרָה־\rb* \rb enough to|עַד־\rb* \rb die|מָֽוֶת׃\rb*!”
\p \v 10 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb cared|חַ֙סְתָּ֙\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the plant|הַקִּ֣יקָי֔וֹן\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb you neither|לֹא־\rb* \rb tended|עָמַ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb made grow|גִדַּלְתּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb It sprang up|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in a night|שֶׁבִּן־\rb*\rb |לַ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb and perished|אָבָֽד׃\rb* \rb in a night|וּבִן־\rb*\rb |לַ֥יְלָה\rb*. \v 11 \rb So should I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb care|אָח֔וּס\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Nineveh|נִינְוֵ֖ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb more than|הַרְבֵּה֩\rb* \rb 120,000|מִֽשְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb*\rb |רִבּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb people|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb tell|יָדַע֙\rb*\rb |בֵּין־\rb* \rb their right hand|יְמִינ֣וֹ\rb* \rb from their left|לִשְׂמֹאל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and many|רַבָּֽה׃\rb* \rb cattle as well|וּבְהֵמָ֖ה\rb*?”
